# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository.
#
# Without this, files committed from Windows carry CRLF, and every checkout on
# Linux (CI, Docker builds, the pilot server) reports the whole tree as modified
# — which is what made `git status` list ~350 changed files with no real changes.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; it stores LF and checks out using
# each developer's core.autocrlf setting, so Windows editors still see CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows checkouts — a CRLF shebang line
# fails with "bad interpreter" inside a container.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Lockfiles are generated; never merge them by hand.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated

# Binary: never touch, never diff.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
